<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bluefields</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bluefields is a port town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast of Nicaragua, at the mouth of the Escondido River. Named after a 17th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> pirate, it became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miskito">Miskito</a> kings under British protection and then of the self-governing Mosquito Reserve created in 1860. Nicaraguan troops occupied it in 1894, and it is now the capital of the South Caribbean Coast Autonomous Region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bluefields.jpg" alt="Bluefields" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ridiculopathy · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historical_Museum_of_Afro-descendants,_Bluefields,_Nicaragua_09.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
